  "explanations": [
   {
    "attribute": "arrangement",
    "likely_right_file": "bhel/Part1.pdf",
    "likely_right_page": 43,
    "why": "Both 2W+1S (two working, one standby) and 3X50% (three pumps at 50% system capacity each) actually describe the exact same design setup, though 2W+1S is explicitly stated in two separate equipment specification sections (Part1 p.43 and Part4 p.59). Running all three together is an operational change from this 100% design flow (2 x 50%) to 150% flow.",
    "consequence": "Because the system was sized for two working pumps (100% capacity, or 250 m3/hr total), running all three pumps together (150% capacity, or 375 m3/hr) may overload the electrical supply, exceed downstream piping pressure or flow limits, and leave no backup if a pump fails during high sump level."
   }
